Layout guardrail screenshot baselines — regeneration log.

Editing this file and pushing runs .github/workflows/layout-baselines.yml
against the branch you pushed, which regenerates the baselines ON THE CI RUNNER
and commits the PNGs back to that branch. It is the trigger that works from any
branch, including one cut before the workflow reached main; once the workflow is
on main, `gh workflow run layout-baselines.yml --ref <branch> -f reason="..."`
does the same thing without touching this file.

Add a dated line saying WHY, newest last. An accepted baseline is an accepted
layout — the line here and the image diff in the PR are the record of who
accepted it.

- 2026-08-01 — First generation. Card 2.3.51 adds the guardrail; /dashboard and
  /account have no committed pictures yet, so CI is failing on missing
  snapshots until this run produces them.
- 2026-08-01 — 320px only. The first run produced 768 and 1280 but never
  reached a screenshot at 320: the suite waited on the <nav> element, and in
  its bar arrangement the nav's only child is `fixed`, leaving the <nav> with a
  zero-height box that Playwright rightly calls invisible. The suite now waits
  on a nav LINK, which is on screen in both arrangements.
